    "narrative": "Heading into today\u2019s slate, our offensive engine is anchored by **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Josh Naylor**, who boast the highest efficiency scores of 69.49 and 64.20, respectively. **Vinnie Pasquantino** draws an excellent matchup against Rocker, where a 14% boost from his platoon advantage and a favorable SP xERA of 4.30 create a prime environment for production. **James Wood** (62.98) also emerges as a high-upside play; despite facing the tough arm of King, his leadoff spot and impressive 0.384 xwOBA profile him as a focal point for our stolen base pursuit. Similarly, **Brice Turang** earns a strong start (60.94) against Lambert, benefiting from a clean lineup spot and moderate SP skill, keeping him firmly in our daily rotation as we aggressively chase the scarcest category of SB.\n\nThe decision to bench **Alex Freeland** (35.63) and **Dalton Rushing** (33.58) highlights the discipline of our current cap-management strategy. Both players struggled to clear the sub-40 floor due to unfavorable matchups against the 3.28 xERA of Luzardo, compounded by bottom-of-the-order projections. **Alex Freeland** was the closest to making the cut, but the optimizer ultimately opted for the higher-upside profiles of **Cole Young** and **Kyle Karros** to maximize our daily total. Meanwhile, we remain cautious regarding the pending lineups for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Corbin Carroll**, and **Jose Caballero**. While **Corbin Carroll** holds a respectable 59.57 score, the presence of Woo on the mound\u2014an elite arm with a 3.43 xERA\u2014coupled with a park penalty, necessitates a close watch to ensure these players remain in optimal lineup slots before first pitch. We continue to monitor the statuses of **Trevor Story** and **Mickey Moniak** on the IL, as their absence forces us to squeeze every drop of efficiency from the active roster.",
